       "type": "text",
       "text": "Before I enter this, I want to check the dose. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg/day, which is about twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 3200 mg/day. A single 1600 mg dose is also above the usual single-dose maximum of 800 mg. At these doses the main risks are GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3200 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n- **400 mg by mouth four times daily** (1600 mg/day, a common inpatient dose)\n- **1600 mg by mouth three times daily** (4800 mg/day, still above the labeled maximum)\n\nIf 1600 mg four times daily is intended, tell me and I'll enter it as written. I can also add a note documenting the rationale, such as the indication or that you reviewed the dose."
      }
